From: Dustin Kirkland <dustin.kirkland@chainguard.dev>
Subject: configure: keep the universal filter without Ghostscript

configure disabled the universal filter whenever Ghostscript was absent
and CUPS_PDFTOPS was empty -- but CUPS_PDFTOPS is never set, so
--disable-ghostscript always meant no universal filter, even with
--enable-universal-cups-filter. The universal filter is libcupsfilters'
cfFilterUniversal(), which renders PDF to raster with pdftoraster
(poppler's pdftoppm) when built without Ghostscript.
---
diff --git a/configure.ac b/configure.ac
index e77cb4b..db71883 100644
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -323,9 +323,6 @@ AC_ARG_ENABLE([universal-cups-filter],
 	[enable_universal_cups_filter="$enableval"],
 	[enable_universal_cups_filter=yes]
 )
-AS_IF([test "x$CUPS_GHOSTSCRIPT" = "x" -a "x$CUPS_PDFTOPS" = "x"], [
-	enable_universal_cups_filter=no
-])
 AM_CONDITIONAL([ENABLE_UNIVERSAL_CUPS_FILTER],
 [test "x$enable_universal_cups_filter" != "xno"])
 
